              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.6: Red rose petals immersed in hot water"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.166,
            0.545,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.3: Let us prepare"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.201,
            0.619,
            0.313
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Collect some fallen petals of red roses available in your surroundings (Fig.  2.5). It is advised not to pluck flowers. You may pick petals or flowers fallen on the ground."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.316,
            0.617,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a fistful of the collected petals of red roses and wash them with water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.378,
            0.617,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Crush the petals using a mortar and pestle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.42,
            0.593,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Place them in a glass tumbler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.63,
            0.184,
            0.886,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.63,
                0.184,
                0.886,
                0.379
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.687,
                0.383,
                0.835,
                0.401
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.5: Red roses"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.445,
            0.883,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pour some hot water into the glass tumbler to ensure that the crushed flower petals are completely immersed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.218,
            0.482,
            0.258,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.218,
                0.482,
                0.258,
                0.51
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.486,
            0.82,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Caution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " — Perform this step under the supervision of an adult."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.507,
            0.883,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cover the glass tumbler with a lid. Wait for 5 – 10 minutes till the water becomes coloured (Fig. 2.6), and filter it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.548,
            0.883,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The filtrate (liquid after filtration) is the required flower extract (Fig. 2.7) to be used as an acid-base indicator."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
